@page RN12 Release notes for VIPR 1.2

Features:
-----------
- check each derivation with empty assumptionlist while processing the DER section, terminating early if RTP is proven
- make error messages more descriptive
- issue warning if the numbers in the labels are not consistent with the internal VIPR counter

Build system
------------
- make Release Mode the default CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE

Fixed bugs
-----------
- allow comments at end of line in viprchk
- allow empty and pure comment lines in viprcomp
- add lazy canonicalization to fix unsuccessful domination checks
- remove compactification marker as source of unsuccessful domination checks
- use global bound changes from the DER section (marked with "global") to complete weak derivations in viprcomp
- terminate viprcomp with an error if a derivation cannot be completed instead of writing an invalid certificate
- viprchk: reject rounding (rnd) of a constraint with a nonzero coefficient on a continuous variable
- viprchk: reject unsplitting (uns) on a disjunction a x <= b | a x >= b + 1 with fractional b
- viprchk: check constraint indices of lin/rnd multipliers and uns assumptions also in release builds
- viprchk: reject unsplitting (uns) on a discarded second assumption instead of dereferencing it
- viprchk: canonicalize rationals after reading (e.g. 5/5 or 1/-2), which GMP does not do on stream input
- viprchk: reject rationals with a zero denominator and malformed multiplier lists instead of crashing
- viprchk_parallel: return an error if the final constraint does not prove the RTP
- viprchk_parallel: keep the assumptions of the second branch when unsplitting (uns)
- viprchk_parallel: check every constraint for every solution, not only the constraint with the solution's index
- viprchk_parallel: require a solution to prove a primal bound

Miscellaneous
-----------
- improve log outputs if checking the certificate fails by adding the constraint names
- rewrite sparse vector comparison to reduce calls to compactify()

